      "to": "amara@finchdata.co",
      "subject": "Re: jac-cloud on Kubernetes?",
      "message": "Hi Amara,\n\nThanks for reaching out. Happy to help with your Q4 planning.\n\n1. Yes, jac-cloud can be deployed on your own Kubernetes cluster, including AWS EKS. The runtime is containerized and stateless at the API layer, and we provide a Helm chart for deployment to any standard Kubernetes cluster. EKS is fully supported.\n\n2. Horizontal scaling of walkers is handled through standard Kubernetes mechanisms. Walker execution scales horizontally behind a load balancer, and you can use the Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA) to scale replicas automatically based on load. Graph state lives in a shared database, so replicas require no coordination with each other\u2014you don't need to manage replicas manually beyond configuring HPA thresholds to suit your traffic patterns.\n\nLet us know if you'd like more detail on the Helm chart configuration or HPA setup. We're glad to support your evaluation.\n\nBest,\nThe Jaseci Team"
    },
